                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I purchased this game and refunded it.  Here's the small amount of good and a short story about the bad: The fighting is somewhat smooth and intuitive, you can tell some time was spent on the mechanics however everything else is completely barebones, it's incredibly alpha for $30.\n\n1 sq. kilometer of basically nothing.  There's no reason to explore any of it.  The environment is incredibly boring.  Everytime you get close to buildings or  any structure your oponents (whoever they are)  just come running out of all the buildings in single file.  They then form a half circle and take turns swiping at you.  Somtimes two of them swing at you together.  The animations are very stiff and after a 30 second encounter you spend the next 5 minutes walking in the most boring medieval landspace created since 1990.  \n\nIn fact the only reason this game has 1 square kilometer is to hold the pair of balls the developer(s?) must have for charging 30 dollars for this.\n\nSee push for emor.  Forever Early Access... this seems to be more of a resume than a game.  Sorry for the harsh review but this thing needs a couple of years of TLC and a whole team to create a bunch of items, lighting, music, sounds, stories, textures, NPCs, lootables...and the list continues, this game needs a kickstarter or some real cash, not an early access release.",
